{"parentUuid":"288b5b0e-e58a-4e9f-83d4-06872c85ef28","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WQP7MGyS66nEwnJr4nNNjY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjJScS51YnEditbwoXhRho","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Rust SAT solver bindings cadical-sys kissat-rs scip-rs 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7417,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":338,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7417},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7417,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxpFERGHQvnugTJBSqD","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"24daa2d8-9a19-4e2e-a8d0-535ec78462cd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:26.856Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cf307adb-2fcd-4318-8a98-a0de582678a8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PFZnm3tbxyZ4kawHcCgkVx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PySAT latest version 2025 2026 PyPI new features\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"pysat\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/pysat/\"},{\"title\":\"python-sat · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/python-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pysathq/pysat: A toolkit for SAT-based prototyping in Python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Features\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/features/\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python - Updates\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/updates/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · pysat/pysat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysat/pysat/releases\"},{\"title\":\"pysat · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/pysat/0.4.4/\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: SAT technology in Python\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Release Notes — pysat 3.2.2 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysat.readthedocs.io/en/latest/release_notes.html\"},{\"title\":\"pysat/README.rst at master · pysathq/pysat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/README.rst\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I found information about PySAT, though it's important to note that there are actually two different projects with similar names:\n\n## PySAT (SAT Solver Toolkit)\n\nThe latest development version is python_sat-1.9.dev2, which was uploaded on March 5, 2026. This version is available on PyPI under the package name \"python-sat\".\n\n### Key Features:\n\nPySAT is a Python toolkit which aims at providing a simple and unified interface to a number of state-of-art Boolean satisfiability (SAT) solvers as well as to a variety of cardinality and pseudo-Boolean encodings.\n\nRecent features and updates include:\n\n- PySAT supports arbitrary Boolean formulas with on-the-fly clausification and provides (pre-)processing functionality by exposing an interface to CaDiCaL's (version 1.5.3) preprocessor\n- Support for CaDiCaL 1.9.5\n- Added Kissat 4.0.4\n- Added functionality to manipulate arbitrary Boolean formulas\n- Added module engines supporting external propagators\n\nPySAT is being developed with the rolling release model, which means many small and frequent updates are provided rather than major releases from time to time.\n\n## PyDat (Python Satellite Data Analysis Toolkit)\n\nNote: The search results also returned information about a different project called \"pysat\" (Python Satellite Data Analysis Toolkit), which is unrelated to the SAT solver toolkit. The latest stable version of this package appears to be 3.2.2, which is focused on satellite data analysis rather than SAT solving.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"47bb5e0c-faa1-45ef-89ad-c7ac9ea0b0c2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:32.343Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf307adb-2fcd-4318-8a98-a0de582678a8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f1b2028a-fabc-4d69-8a7e-bd507179650c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FSHHoyPdcUNaEBYrG9eJar","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy 2025 latest release Pumpkin backend Glasgow constraint solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - CPMpy/cpmpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling library in Python, based on numpy, with direct solver access. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpmpy/\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.gcs — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/pumpkin/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/gcs.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ConSol-Lab/Pumpkin: A Lazy Clause Generation Constraint Programming solver written in Rust. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pumpkin interface (cpmpy.solvers.pumpkin) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/solvers/pumpkin.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling in Python — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/releases\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy Release 0.9.24 Tias Guns Oct 06, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/_/downloads/en/latest/pdf/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - mmcilree/gcspy: A python interface for the Glasgow Constraint Solver, a CP solver implemented as part of research into pseudo-Boolean proof-logging and auditable constraint solving.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mmcilree/gcspy\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy cpo interface (cpmpy.solvers.cpo) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/pumpkin/api/solvers/cpo.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CPMpy and its supported solvers:\n\n## CPMpy and Solver Integration\n\nCPMpy can translate to a wide variety of constraint solving paradigms including CP Solvers: OR-Tools (default), IBM CP Optimizer, Choco, Glasgow GCS, Pumpkin, and MiniZinc+solvers.\n\n## Latest CPMpy Release Information\n\nThe current documented version is CPMpy 0.9.24, released on October 6, 2025.\n\n## Solver-Specific Details\n\n**Pumpkin Backend:**\nPumpkin is a combinatorial optimisation solver developed by the ConSol Lab at TU Delft based on the (lazy clause generation) constraint programming paradigm. The Pumpkin solver in CPMpy supports global constraints including 'InDomain', 'abs', 'alldifferent', 'cumulative', 'div', 'element', 'max', 'min', 'negative_table', 'no_overlap', and 'table'.\n\n**Glasgow Constraint Solver:**\nThe Glasgow Constraint Solver's key feature is the ability to produce proof logs. CPMpy participated in both the 2024 and 2025 XCSP3 competition, twice making its solvers win 3 gold and 1 silver medal.\n\nThe search results confirm that both the Pumpkin and Glasgow constraint solvers are actively supported in CPMpy's latest release.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"32e72e68-d806-40b0-9f17-c21f78dd6700","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:32.638Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1b2028a-fabc-4d69-8a7e-bd507179650c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"24daa2d8-9a19-4e2e-a8d0-535ec78462cd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjJScS51YnEditbwoXhRho","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Rust SAT solver bindings cadical-sys kissat-rs scip-rs 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"rustsat::solvers - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/rustsat/latest/rustsat/solvers/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"cadical_sys - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical-sys\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - chrjabs/rustsat: This library aims to provide implementations of elements commonly used in the development on software in the area of satisfiability solving. The focus of the library is to provide as much ease of use without giving up on performance. GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chrjabs/rustsat\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - mmaroti/cadical-rs: Rust bindings for the CaDiCaL SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mmaroti/cadical-rs\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - UncombedCoconut/cat_solver: Rust bindings for the Kissat SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/UncombedCoconut/cat_solver\"},{\"title\":\"cadical_sys/ lib.rs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical-sys/latest/src/cadical_sys/lib.rs.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - firefighterduck/kissat-rs: Rust bindings for the Kissat SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/firefighterduck/kissat-rs\"},{\"title\":\"cat_solver - crates.io: Rust Package Registry\",\"url\":\"https://crates.io/crates/cat_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - sirandreww/cadical-sys: Unsafe system level bindings of the cadical sat solver written in C++\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sirandreww/cadical-sys\"},{\"title\":\"RustSAT: A Library For SAT Solving in Rust\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.15221v1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Rust SAT solver bindings:\n\n## CaDiCaL Bindings (cadical-sys)\n\ncadical-sys provides Rust bindings for the CaDiCaL SAT Solver, offering low-level access to one of the most efficient Boolean Satisfiability solving libraries. cadical-sys offers complete Rust bindings to the CaDiCaL SAT solver using the cxx crate, enabling seamless interoperability between Rust and C++ SAT solving capabilities.\n\n## Kissat Bindings (kissat-rs)\n\nkissat-rs provides high-level access to the Kissat SAT solver and builds on the lower-level crate kissat-sys. kissat-rs implements a subset of the provided functionalities of Kissat through safe Rust functions on a Solver type that wraps the actual Kissat solver.\n\n## RustSAT Library (2025)\n\nCurrently interfaces are available for cadical, kissat, glucose, and minisat through the RustSAT library. RustSAT provides crates for the state-of-the-art SAT solvers Kissat, CaDiCaL, MiniSat, and Glucose.\n\nNote: Regarding SCIP-rs specifically, the search results did not contain information about scip-rs bindings in 2025. The results focus on the major Rust SAT solver bindings available through RustSAT and other community projects.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"86ab4ba7-e212-4fdd-882c-e3f541e59a5f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:32.800Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"24daa2d8-9a19-4e2e-a8d0-535ec78462cd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"288b5b0e-e58a-4e9f-83d4-06872c85ef28","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VvWcVWqwCz4GqixyuJHGVo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"python-mip Pyomo cvxpy 2025 release status maintenance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cvxpy - Python Package Health Analysis | Snyk\",\"url\":\"https://snyk.io/advisor/python/cvxpy\"},{\"title\":\"Meta-ticket: Use Python optimization interfaces: CVXPY, SCIP, or-tools, PuLP, Pyomo, cylp... · Issue #26511 · sagemath/sage\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sagemath/sage/issues/26511\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Optimization modelling in Python\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/resources/links/optimization-modelling-in-python\"},{\"title\":\"Cvxpy\",\"url\":\"https://www.cvxpy.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Related Projects — Pyomo\",\"url\":\"https://www.pyomo.org/related-projects\"},{\"title\":\"Optimisation with Pyomo – datawookie’s blog\",\"url\":\"https://datawookie.dev/blog/2024/12/optimisation-with-pyomo/\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmarking Six Python Optimization Frameworks in a Head-to-Head Performance Test | by Kyle Jones | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@kyle-t-jones/benchmarking-six-python-optimization-frameworks-in-a-head-to-head-performance-test-4836c61a65a1\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · cvxpy/cvxpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvxpy/cvxpy/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Solver Max - Python-MIP\",\"url\":\"https://www.solvermax.com/resources/links/optimization-modelling-in-python/python-mip\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing with Pyomo: A Complete Step-by-Step Guide | DataCamp\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/pyomo\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the release status and maintenance of these Python optimization libraries:\n\n## CVXPY\n\nCVXPY demonstrates a positive version release cadence with at least one new version released in the past 3 months, and its maintenance status is considered healthy. The current version supports Python 3.11 through 3.14, CVXPY 1.8 will be supported with bugfixes while developing the 1.9 release, and CVXPY 1.7 and older are no longer supported. CVXPY added the open source solver HiGHS as its default mixed-integer linear programming (MILP) solver.\n\n## Pyomo\n\nThe search results confirm that Pyomo is a flexible open source optimization modeling language for Python that can be used to define, solve, and analyze a wide range of optimization problems, including Linear Programming (LP) and Mixed-Integer Programming (MIP), nonlinear programming (NLP), and differential equations. However, the search results don't provide specific 2025 release status information.\n\n## Python-MIP\n\nPython-MIP is a collection of Python tools for the modeling and solution of Mixed-Integer Linear programs (MIPs), and its syntax was inspired by PuLP but provides access to advanced solver features like cut generation, lazy constraints, MIP starts and solution pools. The search results don't provide specific 2025 release or maintenance status information for Python-MIP.\n\nThe search results don't contain detailed information about recent 2025 releases for Pyomo and Python-MIP specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"59d8b446-0cc2-429c-9fb9-6cdc2bf366fe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:33.018Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"288b5b0e-e58a-4e9f-83d4-06872c85ef28","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
