ws that MathOptInterface.jl is the core optimization interface that provides a unified interface to mathematical optimization solvers.\n\nRecent updates include support for vector-valued objective functions, a Utilities.distance_to_set method for SecondOrderCone, and improved constraint bridges so that Bridges.final_touch can be called multiple times without forcing a rebuild of the reformulation.\n\n## Documentation Status\n\nThe MathOptInterface documentation was generated with Documenter.jl version 1.16.1 on Friday 30 January 2026, indicating current documentation is available as of early 2026.\n\nThe search results provide information about the MathOptInterface library structure and recent improvements, but the specific detailed version numbering for all 2025 releases would require checking the official GitHub releases page or version history directly, which you can access at the MathOptInterface GitHub repository releases page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2bf6fddd-1c5f-43ca-a1b3-9f4a690301a7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:42.733Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8d59919-136c-40b1-8e6b-187813038b41","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8467fc05-5b16-476d-9dc7-896c013eb995","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SN8kR6dc6PpJg2syYAwdDr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PyO3 pybind11 2025 SAT solver bindings Python Rust\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - PyO3/pyo3: Rust bindings for the Python interpreter · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started - PyO3 user guide\",\"url\":\"https://pyo3.rs/v0.10.1/\"},{\"title\":\"PyO3: Rust Bindings for the Python Interpreter | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=25956502\"},{\"title\":\"PyO3: Python Rust binding | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=14859844\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - AndrejOrsula/pyo3_bindgen: Automatic Python —> Rust FFI bindings\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/AndrejOrsula/pyo3_bindgen\"},{\"title\":\"How I published my 1st Rust-Python binding package | by Senhaji Rhazi hamza | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://hamza-senhajirhazi.medium.com/how-i-published-my-1st-rust-python-binding-package-cb44bc4e2e94\"},{\"title\":\"Creating multiple constructors & shorter bindings (similar to pybind11) · Issue #4356 · PyO3/pyo3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3/issues/4356\"},{\"title\":\"pyo3 - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/pyo3\"},{\"title\":\"Creating multiple constructors & shorter bindings (similar to pybind11) · PyO3/pyo3 · Discussion #4357\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3/discussions/4357\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - PyO3 user guide\",\"url\":\"https://pyo3.rs/v0.12.3/\"}]\n\nI found search results about PyO3 and pybind11 as Python-Rust binding tools. However, the search results don't contain specific information about SAT solver bindings or 2025-specific developments. Here's what I found:\n\n## PyO3 and pybind11 Overview\n\nPyO3 can be used to write a native Python module in Rust, or to embed Python in a Rust binary. The easiest way to use PyO3 for the first time is to use maturin, a tool for building and publishing Rust-based Python packages with minimal configuration.\n\nThe search results show that PyO3 bindings contain significant boilerplate and are much longer compared to pybind11, with some developers asking how to achieve a similar level of conciseness as pybind11.\n\n## Key Differences\n\nThe results also document discussions about creating Python bindings, with comparisons showing that there is no such thing as multiple constructors in Python, so pybind11 probably creates a wrapper in the background calling constructors based on types received, which can be mimicked by taking arguments and typechecking.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about SAT solver bindings for Python/Rust or recent developments in 2025. To find more targeted information on that topic, you may want to search specifically for \"SAT solver Python Rust\" or look for projects on GitHub that combine SAT solving with Python bindings.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6d418447-9aae-42de-8cb8-a8ed2503c319","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:43.045Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8467fc05-5b16-476d-9dc7-896c013eb995","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0c26dcb0-61ca-4b08-b4ba-f62032625b5c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BmmexLA1xZK5K7PhE2ovZD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-tools Python typing async asyncio CP-SAT 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Mastering Python's typing.Coroutine: Pitfalls and Async Alternatives\",\"url\":\"https://runebook.dev/en/docs/python/library/typing/typing.Coroutine\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Guide to Asynchronous Programming in Python | Better Stack Community\",\"url\":\"https://betterstack.com/community/guides/scaling-python/python-async-programming/\"},{\"title\":\"asyncio — Asynchronous I/O\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/asyncio.html\"},{\"title\":\"asyncio in Python - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/asyncio-in-python/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - timofurrer/awesome-asyncio: A curated list of awesome Python asyncio frameworks, libraries, software and resources · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/timofurrer/awesome-asyncio\"},{\"title\":\"A Conceptual Overview of asyncio — Python 3.14.5rc1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3/howto/a-conceptual-overview-of-asyncio.html\"},{\"title\":\"asyncio | Python Standard Library – Real Python\",\"url\":\"https://realpython.com/ref/stdlib/asyncio/\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py\"},{\"title\":\"Python Asyncio Part 3 – Asynchronous Context Managers and Asynchronous Iterators | cloudfit-public-docs\",\"url\":\"https://bbc.github.io/cloudfit-public-docs/asyncio/asyncio-part-3.html\"},{\"title\":\"Python's asyncio: A Hands-On Walkthrough – Real Python\",\"url\":\"https://realpython.com/async-io-python/\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query. The results primarily cover Python's asyncio library, typing with coroutines, and asynchronous programming concepts. However, the search results don't contain significant information specifically about OR-tools CP-SAT solver with async/asyncio support or recent 2025 developments.\n\nHere's what the search returned:\n\n**Python asyncio and typing:**\n- The typing.Coroutine type hint is used by type checkers (like Mypy or Pyright) to specify the types related to a coroutine function.\n- asyncio is a library to write concurrent code using the async/await syntax.\n- Async I/O is a single-threaded, single-process technique that uses cooperative multitasking.\n\n**OR-tools:**\nThe search found a reference to the OR-tools GitHub repository (Google's Operations Research tools), specifically the CP-SAT solver's Python module, but didn't return detailed documentation about async support or 2025 updates.\n\nIf you're looking for specific information about:\n- Async/await support in OR-tools CP-SAT\n- Type hints in OR-tools Python bindings\n- Recent 2025 updates to OR-tools\n\nI'd recommend checking the official OR-tools documentation or GitHub repository directly, as the web search results didn't capture those specific details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a5a8c50d-476c-4e23-ab36-956af376ffdc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:43.673Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0c26dcb0-61ca-4b08-b4ba-f62032625b5c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
