{"parentUuid":"b53ef64c-3a60-41a3-9bf2-1843b69c15e4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GTwerRCmE26adPUWfbbC89","type":"tool_result","content":"# python-sat PyPI Package Summary\n\n**Latest Stable Version:** Not currently available. The most recent release is version **1.9.dev2** (pre-release), dated March 5, 2026.\n\n**Release Activity:** The package shows extensive development activity, with numerous pre-release versions deployed throughout 2024-2026. Based on the release history provided, there have been approximately **50+ pre-release versions** issued during this period, demonstrating continuous development and iteration.\n\n**Package Purpose:** This is \"A Python library providing a simple interface to a number of state-of-art Boolean satisfiability (SAT) solvers\" with support for cardinality and pseudo-Boolean encodings, enabling researchers to prototype SAT-based applications efficiently.\n\n**Key Details:**\n- **License:** MIT\n- **Maintainer:** Alexey Ignatiev (aign)\n- **Repository:** https://github.com/pysathq/pysat\n- **Python Support:** Compatible with Python 3.8 through 3.14"}]},"uuid":"adfa175d-2b12-4387-8743-ab73639036f4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:06.349Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b53ef64c-3a60-41a3-9bf2-1843b69c15e4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d7e80cef-4e1b-4314-9842-5f1985b64de2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VkpqBejEvYcAWbWBbjEzBc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-tools CP-SAT 9.13 9.14 2025 2026 release Python typing stubs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Issues with CP-SAT python type annotations · Issue #4120 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4120\"},{\"title\":\"ortools · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ortools/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools 9.7.2996\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ortools/9.7.2996/\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about OR-tools releases related to CP-SAT and Python typing:\n\nPython CP-SAT type hints were added via pull request #3668, which represents work on improving the typing support for the CP-SAT solver.\n\nRegarding specific version releases, version 9.13.4784 was released on June 6, 2025, and version 9.14.6206 was released on June 19, 2025. Additionally, version 9.15.6755 was uploaded on January 14, 2026.\n\nVersion 9.9.3963 included some py.typed files, indicating early support for Python type annotations in the package.\n\nThe search results show that OR-tools has been actively improving its Python typing support across recent releases, with work on both type hints and typing stub files to enhance the development experience for Python users.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f1ac6981-cd76-4968-a7c0-7ab7b11344bc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:07.489Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d7e80cef-4e1b-4314-9842-5f1985b64de2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"78fb4b7c-d57d-4442-be82-2a12f650f527","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuGWmcJ2Q5rrzsYVije5xw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"python-mip\" 1.16 release 2025 maintained dead\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Goodbye python-mip? - Richard Oberdieck\",\"url\":\"https://oberdieck.dk/2024/11/12/goodbye-python-mip/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · coin-or/python-mip\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/coin-or/python-mip/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · coin-or/python-mip\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/coin-or/python-mip/issues\"},{\"title\":\"mip - Python Package Health Analysis | Snyk\",\"url\":\"https://snyk.io/advisor/python/mip\"},{\"title\":\"Python-MIP\",\"url\":\"https://www.python-mip.com/\"},{\"title\":\"[QUESTION] conda-forge release? · Issue #56 · coin-or/python-mip\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/coin-or/python-mip/issues/56\"},{\"title\":\"Python | endoflife.date\",\"url\":\"https://endoflife.date/python\"},{\"title\":\"Python 3.12 · Issue #376 · coin-or/python-mip\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/coin-or/python-mip/issues/376\"},{\"title\":\"Python MIP (Mixed-Integer Linear Programming) Tools\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/mip/\"},{\"title\":\"python-mip/mip/model.py at master · coin-or/python-mip\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/coin-or/python-mip/blob/master/mip/model.py\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding python-mip:\n\n**Release History:**\nThere is no version 1.16 of python-mip. The latest release prior to recent updates was 1.15.0, which came in January 2023. However, more recent versions have been released: version 1.17.6 has been released, indicating the project is still active.\n\n**Maintenance Status:**\nThe maintenance situation is nuanced. Earlier concerns existed: the latest commit to master was in May 2024 as of November 2024. However, more recent activity shows the project has continued: python-mip 1.17 ships with full support for HiGHS — a high-performance, open-source LP/MIP solver, and python-mip 1.17.1 was released, suggesting ongoing maintenance into 2025.\n\n**Current Status:**\nWhile one source noted that the package hasn't seen any new versions released to PyPI in the past 12 months and could be considered as discontinued, this appears to be outdated information given the 1.17.x releases. Multiple issues have been opened on the GitHub repository in 2025, indicating ongoing community engagement.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7cca6cac-c941-4705-9abd-4a5e84aafb37","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:08.126Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"78fb4b7c-d57d-4442-be82-2a12f650f527","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a5115454-8451-4902-a097-8a6777f3ec58","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B79y5oTeBNuurhHJfwqcwC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy vs PySAT comparison 2025 Boolean encoding hybrid solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.pysat — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/pytest_all_solvers_versions_tool/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.pysat — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/version-checking/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/blocks_world/api/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Modeling and solving with CPMpy — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/modeling.html\"},{\"title\":\"OptiLog V2: Model, Solve, Tune and Run Josep Alòs !\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol236-sat2022/LIPIcs.SAT.2022.25/LIPIcs.SAT.2022.25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solvers — CPMpy 0.5 documentation - Read the Docs\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy Release 0.9.24 Tias Guns Oct 06, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/_/downloads/en/latest/pdf/\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/docs/solvers.md at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/docs/solvers.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CPMpy's integration with PySAT rather than a direct 2025 comparison. Here's what I found:\n\n## CPMpy and PySAT Integration\n\nPySAT is a Python toolkit which aims at providing a simple and unified interface to a number of state-of-art Boolean satisfiability (SAT) solvers as well as to a variety of cardinality and pseudo-Boolean encodings.\n\nCPMpy's default solver is OR-Tools CP-SAT, but CPMpy supports multiple other solvers including SAT solvers (those in PySAT), the Z3 SMT solver, a conflict-driven cutting-planes solver (Exact), and any CP solver supported by the text-based MiniZinc language.\n\n## Key Differences\n\n**PySAT Limitations:** The PySAT solver can only be used if the model only uses Boolean variables and does not support optimization.\n\n**Boolean Encoding:** CPMpy offers encoding options for int2bool, with choices from \"auto\", \"direct\", \"order\", or \"binary\".\n\n**Incrementality:** Gurobi and the PySAT solvers are fully incremental, as is Z3. This means both support reusing learned clauses across multiple solve calls.\n\n**Core Extraction:** Solution_hint() and get_core() are supported by the OrTools and PySAT solvers and interfaces.\n\nThe search results did not return a specific 2025 comparison paper or benchmark between CPMpy and PySAT. For more recent comparative analysis, you may want to check academic publications or benchmarking studies from 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"474f18ca-ee15-4bba-8f67-21877e6c0294","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:09.565Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a5115454-8451-4902-a097-8a6777f3ec58","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"474f18ca-ee15-4bba-8f67-21877e6c0294","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a053c965da12f63d8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01W3pYEAzPiKbSJsqf9ZpCsy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough comprehensive data. Let me compile the report.\n\n# SAT/CP/MIP Solver Bindings 生态盘点（2024-2026）\n\n## 横向对比\n\n| 工具 | 最新版/日期 | 维护活跃度 | GitHub | 性质 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PySAT (python-sat)** | 1.9.dev2（2026-03-05），rolling release | 高，频繁小版本（50+ pre-release/2024-2026） | 451★，pysathq/pysat | SAT 求解 + 编码统一接口；新增 CaDiCaL 1.9.5、Kissat 4.0.4、external propagators、任意 Bool 公式 |\n| **CPMpy** | 0.10.0（2026-01-19） | 非常高，1888 commits，39 releases | 351★，CPMpy/cpmpy | CP 建模层 + 多 backend；新接 Pumpkin 和 Glasgow GCS（带 proof log），XCSP3 2024/2025 拿 3 金 1 银 |\n| **Pumpkin** (Rust LCG-CP) | 0.3.0（2026-02-11） | 中-高，594 commits，TU Delft 团队 | 74★，consol-lab/pumpkin | Rust 写的 lazy clause generation CP 求解器；MiniZinc 2025 铜牌；带 unsat 证书；有 Python bindings |\n| **RustSAT** | 0.7.5（2026-01-30），158 releases | 高 | 67★，chrjabs/rustsat | Rust 库统一 cadical/kissat/glucose/minisat；带 PyPI Python bindings、VeriPB proof logging |\n| **OR-Tools CP-SAT** | 9.15.6755（2026-01-14） | 极高，Google 维护 | google/or-tools | 我们正在用的；近版本补全 py.typed、PR #3668 加 type hints |\n| **PySCIPOpt** | 6.1.0（2026-02-05），CPython 3.14 wheels | 高，跟 SCIP 同步 | scipopt/PySCIPOpt | SCIP 的 Python 接口，MILP/约束 IP |\n| **CVXPY** | 1.8.x（2026），1.7-停维 | 健康，3 个月内有版本 | cvxpy/cvxpy | Python 3.11-3.14；HiGHS 升级为默认 MILP 求解器 |\n| **python-mip** | 1.17.6（2025） | 中，曾有\"goodbye python-mip\"质疑但仍在更新 | coin-or/python-mip | 1.17 加 HiGHS 支持，但提交节奏慢 |\n| **Pyomo** | 持续维护 | 高，企业/学术大量在用 | Pyomo/pyomo | LP/MIP/NLP/DAE 全谱；重型建模框架 |\n| **JuMP / MathOptInterface** | MOI 1.40+（2026-01 文档） | 极高，Julia 生态主力 | jump-dev | Julia 的统一求解器接口，跟我们 Python 路径无关 |\n\n## 几个值得注意的点\n\n- **PySAT 还活着且活得很好**：rolling release 模式让它看起来\"没有大版本\"，实际 2024-2026 一直在加 solver 和 propagator hooks。\"PySAT 已死、CPMpy 取代\"是误读——CPMpy 的 SAT backend 本身就是包了 PySAT。\n- **CPMpy 是趋势但不是替代**：CPMpy 是 CP 建模层（类似 JuMP 之于 Julia），底下接 OR-Tools/PySAT/Pumpkin/Glasgow/Choco/CPO。它和 PySAT 是**层次关系**不是替代关系。\n- **Pumpkin + Glasgow GCS 是新东西**：2024-2026 才进入 CPMpy 主线，带**证明日志（proof logging）**，这是过去 Python 生态没有的能力。\n- **OR-Tools typing 补全**：9.13+ 加了 py.typed，PR #3668 改进 type hints——以前 IDE 自动补全很差，现在好转。\n- **async/asyncio + solver**：没有原生支持。CP-SAT 仍是阻塞调用，要并发必须靠 multiprocessing（我们已经在用）或自己包 `asyncio.to_thread`。\n- **Rust 路径**（cadical-sys / kissat-rs / RustSAT / Pumpkin）成熟度上升，但要 PyO3 自包；不适合现有 Python 项目轻量接入。\n\n## 对我们项目可借力的 1-2 个工具\n\n**1. CPMpy 0.10 + Glasgow GCS proof logging（强烈推荐评估）**\n我们项目核心痛点就是 `certified_exact` 路径需要可审计的证明源。Glasgow GCS 通过 CPMpy 暴露了 VeriPB pseudo-Boolean proof logs，这正好对应 PROJECT_LOCK.md 里\"certified path 必须有证明基础\"的硬需求。建议在 S6 之后开一个 spike：把 binding subproblem（Boolean-heavy）从 OR-Tools 转写成 CPMpy 模型，跑 GCS backend，看能不能拿到外部可验证的 proof log——这是 OR-Tools CP-SAT 本身给不了的能力。\n\n**2. OR-Tools 9.15 typing 升级（低成本立即收益）**\n当前我们用的 ortools 9.15.6755 已经带 py.typed 和改进的 type hints。值得花半小时跑 mypy 在 `src/models/*.py` 上，把 IDE 警告清理掉，对 AI sidecar（Lane C）写代码有正面收益——CP-SAT API 以前是 stringly-typed，hint 之后能让 AI 建议更准。\n\n**不建议**：迁移到 PySCIPOpt 或 python-mip（不解决我们的 CP 建模需求，且 python-mip 维护风险偏高）；引入 Rust binding（对单基地 70x70 项目过度工程）。\n\nSources:\n- [PySAT PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/python-sat/)\n- [pysathq/pysat GitHub](https://github.com/pysathq/pysat)\n- [CPMpy GitHub](https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy)\n- [CPMpy 0.9.24 docs](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html)\n- [Pumpkin GitHub](https://github.com/consol-lab/pumpkin)\n- [RustSAT GitHub](https://github.com/chrjabs/rustsat)\n- [RustSAT arXiv 2505.15221](https://arxiv.org/html/2505.15221v1)\n- [PySCIPOpt GitHub](https://github.com/scipopt/PySCIPOpt)\n- [PySCIPOpt PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/PySCIPOpt/)\n- [CVXPY Snyk Advisor](https://snyk.io/advisor/python/cvxpy)\n- [python-mip releases](https://github.com/coin-or/python-mip/releases)\n- [Goodbye python-mip - Oberdieck](https://oberdieck.dk/2024/11/12/goodbye-python-mip/)\n- [OR-Tools releases](https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases)\n- [OR-Tools issue #4120 typing](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4120)\n- [MathOptInterface release notes](https://jump.dev/MathOptInterface.jl/stable/release_notes/)\n- [gcspy Glasgow Constraint Solver Python](https://github.com/mmcilree/gcspy)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3920,"cache_read_input_tokens":32863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3920,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxsuztafbazAXthzcQA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"44902cc8-e7bf-41d1-8208-abef69345977","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:55.908Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
